1) Slim invocation prompt

Paste one of these to trigger Aegis. Pick the line that matches your mode.

Review (read-only)

```
aegis review — target: <repo/service> @ <commit/tag>, date <YYYY-MM-DD>. Owner: <name>. Owner-controlled: yes. Active testing: no. Scope: <paths/services/data classes>. Out of scope: <...>. Depth: Standard. Budget: one pass of the ten domains. Read-only — change nothing.
```

Harden (fixes on a branch)

```
aegis harden — target: <repo/service> @ <commit/tag>, date <YYYY-MM-DD>. Owner: <name>. Decider: <name>. Owner-controlled: yes. Active testing: no. Scope: <...>. Out of scope: <...>. Depth: Standard. Branch prefix: aegis/fix-. One cause per patch; each with a regression test that fails unpatched. Do not merge. Hand off anything needing secret rotation, prod config, migration, or DNS.
```

Triage (suspected incident)

```
aegis triage — target: <system>, first-seen <YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MMZ>. Owner: <name>. Decider: <name>. Contact channel: <...>. Authorized to contain: <yes/no; if yes, list pre-approved steps>. Preserve evidence (hash) before changes. Timeline with sources. No attribution speculation. Legal/breach determination is the owner's.
```

Minimal one-liner (if the runner fills in blanks)

```
Run aegis in <Review|Harden|Triage> mode on <target> at <commit/tag>. Owner-controlled, authorization on file. Apply preflight, all ten domains, severity×exposure, evidence tags, and the AEGIS REPORT output contract.
```

Optional flags you can append

· Depth: Surface | Standard | Deep
· Focus: <domain numbers> — e.g. Focus: 2,4,6 to spend budget on authz, secrets, CI
· Advisory source: <OSV | GitHub Advisories | npm | PyPI>, checked <YYYY-MM-DD>
· Report redaction: last-4 (default) or none (still never full secret)

